# What scripts/personal-data-scan.py lets through. One entry per line: kind: value.
# Kinds: email, email-domain (covers subdomains), ip, author (commit author email), path (regex).
# Add an entry only for data that is safe to publish; say why in a comment.

# Commit identities allowed to author commits here (GitHub's users.noreply.github.com addresses
# always pass). Nothing else: a commit by any other address is refused.
